/-!
# A finite certificate for simultaneous F4 root placement

The 48 rows of `coords` are twice the standard real F4 roots, in lexicographic
order. `reflect` records the four simple reflections. Each ordered pair has
`certificate = (distance, i, j)`: at distance zero its simple-root coefficients
vanish outside nodes i and j; otherwise reflection i strictly decreases the
distance. Thus induction constructs one word placing both roots, including
equal and opposite pairs. No word expansion is needed in the certificate check.

All finite assertions are checked by the Lean kernel. The coordinate coverage
and reflection identities below are transported to the literal real root system
in the parent `Placement` module. The distance table was found by breadth-first
search from the standard planes; its generation is not trusted by the proof.

Source: GLS3 §2.9.3, `refs/KGroup/GLS3/chapter2.tex`, lines 1455–1462.
-/

